  {
   "t": 97.77,
   "kind": "thought",
   "data": {
    "text": "In a `120 mm / 3 h` storm over the whole study area `lagos-lekki-v3`:\n\nBaseline `r_cf97d373df9a960d`:\n\n* Whole area: `buildings_flooded` 26114, `road_km_impassable` 353.548, `max_depth_m` 2.068\n* Inside `Lekki-Epe Expressway`:\n  * `area:Lekki-Epe Expressway:road_km_impassable` 32.659 km\n  * `area:Lekki-Epe Expressway:max_depth_m` 1.157 m\n\nCorridor is impassable.\n\n### Smallest effective set tested\n\n1 intervention object, applied city-wide:\n\n> city-wide upgrade of existing drains x3 + city-wide new drainage 40 mm/h\n> `r_409523f5d30bff6a`\n\n```\n[{\"type\":\"drain_upgrade\",\"capacity_factor\":3.0,\"add_mm_h\":40.0}]\n```\n\nNo `place` = whole study area. `add_mm_h` is city-wide new drainage, not a local fix.\n\nResult `r_409523f5d30bff6a`:\n\n* Whole area: `buildings_flooded` 4914, `road_km_impassable` 6.999, `max_depth_m` 0.611\n* Inside `Lekki-Epe Expressway`:\n  * `area:Lekki-Epe Expressway:road_km_impassable` 0.201 km\n  * `area:Lekki-Epe Expressway:max_depth_m` 0.37 m\n  * `area:Lekki-Epe Expressway:buildings_flooded` 50 vs 669 in baseline\n  * `area:Lekki-Epe Expressway:flooded_area_km2` 0.0293 vs 0.7276 in baseline\n\nDifference alt - base `r_409523f5d30bff6a - r_cf97d373df9a960d`:\n\n* `buildings_flooded` -21200\n* `buildings_flooded_severe` -7865\n* `road_km_impassable` -346.549\n* `people_exposed` -74508\n* `flooded_area_km2` -19.3447\n\nThat is ~99.4% reduction on the Expressway impassable length, from 32.659 km to 0.201 km.\n\nEvacuation check at peak `t_s=9000s` in that run from Expressway centroid:\n\n* `rt_0c10c7c141b1` `reachable:true`, 2.739 km, ETA 41.1 min to `Unnamed place of worship (candidate shelter (assumed))`\n\n### Why this is the smallest\n\n* Adding `green in Lekki Phase 1` to the same drains `r_a1b359c618800df3` gives same Expressway result: `area:Lekki-Epe Expressway:road_km_impassable` 0.201 km, `max_depth_m` 0.344 m. No additional benefit on the corridor, so excluded from minimal set.\n* Adding `pond in Open land near Ajah` `r_c7e6ffcd89b046c4` triggered warning: ponds cover 4 buildings - displaces people, not a flood reduction. Not recommended as drawn. Whole-area `road_km_impassable` rose to 8.583 km.\n\nNo single lighter preset was confirmed to reach this level, and run budget is exhausted. Strict `0.000 km` was not achieved in any confirmed run - 0.201 km / 0.37 m max depth remains, essentially one ~200 m section above the 0.3 m passability threshold.\n\nPlanning model, not a forecast."
   }
